  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1058 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nFriday through Monday:\n\nAs the cold front exits to the southeast late Thursday, drier\nair and high pressure is expected to move into Wisconsin. This\nwill bring a period of dry and cool weather across the area \nthrough Saturday. High temperatures are expected to be in the\nlow to mid 60s with overnight lows in the lower to upper 40s.\nFriday night will have the best potential for a chance at see\nsome upper 30 degree temperatures overnight. \n\nLate Saturday into Sunday guidance as a low pressure system\npassing just to the north of the forecast area. The better lift\nand forcing look to remain across northern Wisconsin and Canada.\nMoisture return looks to be very weak too which will further\nlimit the potential for any rain. While very low, opted to keep\nthe 10-15% chance for rain across central Wisconsin as a few\nmembers of guidance do have the sfc low a bit further south. \nThen high pressure returns keeping things cold and dry through \nthe rest of the extended. \n\nPatterson",
